# The DHIS2 versions the dhis2 service runs, oldest first, one per line:
#   <DHIS2 version> <tomcat image tag> <release WAR URL> <WAR SHA-256>
# Every line is an upgrade step: the final patch of its minor version. DHIS2's database migrations
# can't skip versions, and each version needs its Java (dhis2-releases notes): 8 to 2.37, 11 for
# 2.38-40, 17 for 2.41-43. 2.42 and later are Jakarta EE (Servlet 6, Spring 6): they need Tomcat 10.1
# (in Tomcat 9 they deploy but never start; checked 2026-11-23). The tag pins the Tomcat and JDK major
# versions and the Ubuntu release (noble), so `pull` brings Tomcat and Java patches but never a new
# OS release. dhis2-setup checks that an instance's DHIS2_TOMCAT_TAG is its version's tag here.
# (See README.md.)
# URLs and checksums are from https://releases.dhis2.org/v1/versions/stable.json (2026-10-26; 2.41,
# 2.42 and 2.43 on 2026-11-23, where 2.41.11.0 is named 2.41.11), except 2.30's: it isn't in that
# metadata, and https://releases.dhis2.org/2.30/dhis.war is a rolling build of the 2.30 branch
# (b1c3a49, 2021-06-25), its checksum taken from the download. lsdata runs an earlier one (b3863ff,
# 2019-12-06, SHA-256 0e30767d9d29e6fc1d04e70a8353ae88de884d786ab324933de6a49bb67cc8bd) that's no
# longer published; the commits between them change no schema (*.hbm.xml or startup upgrade code),
# only translations and bug fixes (checked 2026-10-26).
